message: "If you find this reference architecture or benchmark useful in your research or engineering projects, citation using the metadata below is welcome and optional."
type: software
title: "ai-layered-control: A Systems-Engineering Reference Architecture for Layered Closed-Loop AI Control"
abstract: "A reference architecture for AI-in-the-loop control that separates slow qualitative supervision from deterministic actuator control. A 10 Hz supervisor selects regimes or abstains using calibrated distance-based confidence. A 1 kHz ANSI C99 core applies input validation, local-clock frame leases, a 32 B residual probe that suppresses the tracking trend while retaining broadband content, independent physical vetoes, tracking anti-windup and bounded fallback without dynamic allocation. The repository provides Python and MCU integration templates, a Simulink C-MEX adapter, and reproducible Python/MATLAB mirror benchmarks, with device-interface examples for robotics, wire-arc additive manufacturing and neuromodulation."
